{
  "id": 437724314,
  "iid": 22586,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Add extern \"C\" for C++ compatibility",
  "description": "`epan/reassemble.h` and `epan/ptvcursor.h` didn't have `extern \"C\"` for public\nfunction which resulted in attempt to link C++ mangled names when used\nfrom C++ source file.\n\nFor `reassemble.h` it was possible to wrap `#include` in `extern \"C\"` but\n`ptvcursor.h` proved more difficult - `packet.h` includes glib header that,\nwhen in C++ and on Win32 used` template<>` which is a failure when in `extern\n\"C\"` block.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-12-03T10:35:04.354Z",
